<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<!--
    Foreground layer: the brand play mark in accent #50D5DA.
    
    The path is the same as on Apple (`Marken.signetForm`, unchanged, in its own 1024 x 1024 box).
    Not redrawn: a hand-built shape would be a second logo.
    
    Safe zone: an adaptive icon is a 108 x 108 dp box of which the system only guarantees the inner
    72 x 72; the outer 18 dp per side go to the mask and parallax. Apple shows the whole 1024 tile.
    To make the mark look equally large on both, the 1024 box is mapped onto exactly those 72:
    
        scale   72 / 1024       = 0.0703125
        offset  (108 - 72) / 2  = 18
    
    The shape (x 321.6 to 754.6, y 280 to 744 in the 1024 box) ends up 30.5 x 32.6 dp, 42 % and 45 %
    of the visible 72, as on Apple, and sits fully inside the safe zone (18 to 90). Apple's slight
    shift to the right stays: a play triangle looks centred when it sits a bit right of the
    geometric middle.
    
    `<group>` applies scale before offset (M = T * S), so the two numbers above are used as they
    are, with no converted path points.
-->
<vector xmlns:android="http://schemas.android.com/apk/res/android"
    android:width="108dp" android:height="108dp"
    android:viewportWidth="108" android:viewportHeight="108">
    <group android:scaleX="0.0703125" android:scaleY="0.0703125"
           android:translateX="18" android:translateY="18">
        <path android:fillColor="#50D5DA"
              android:pathData="M440.1,280l285,163.2c38,21.7,51.2,70,29.6,108-7,12.3-17.2,22.5-29.6,29.6l-285,163.2c-37.9,21.8-86.3,8.6-108.1-29.3-6.9-12-10.5-25.6-10.5-39.4v-326.6c0-43.7,35.5-79.2,79.2-79.2,13.8,0,27.4,3.6,39.4,10.5Z" />
    </group>
</vector>
